hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-42 = cons "The claim to universality has a precise content." (cons "" (cons "**Every existing graph embeds.** A triple is a degenerate construction: a relation type whose inhabitant carries" (cons "no rationale beyond its assertion. A property graph is a family of such types with attributes. An OWL ontology is a" (cons "type theory of a restricted kind, and its entailments are constructions. A probabilistic knowledge base is a graph" (cons "plus a supplied probability structure, which §1 treats as additional information. Every current format can be" (cons "represented in hyperactivity without loss, and its semantics become explicit where they were implicit." (cons "" nil)))))))
